{
  "format": 1,
  "name": "plumbing_flood",
  "spec": ["plumbing 6", "plumbing 6.1", "plumbing 6.2", "plumbing 6.3", "plumbing 6.4", "plumbing 6.5", "plumbing 6.6", "plumbing 6.7", "plumbing 14.9", "plumbing 14.10"],
  "description": "Test 9: pump of 1000 at (5,5) (water at (5,4)), pipes x = 5..9 at z = 5 connected along x, a consumer of 300 at (12,5). One network: the pass takes 2N + 7 = 9 DoIdle calls. Ring 0 is the pipe row; rings 1-3 grow by Chebyshev distance (radius 7 >> 1 = 3), rings 4-6 by Manhattan steps, so a cell is watered when 3 + max(0,|dx|-3) + max(0,|dz|-3) <= 6 (distance to the nearest pipe cell): (12,5) ring 3, (12,8) ring 3, (15,5) ring 6 watered; (16,5) ring 7 not. Published values: the consumer lot 1 | 2 = 3, pipes 8 | 1 = 9, the pump lot 8 | 1 | 2 | 4 = 15. Pass consumed 300, own production 1000, ratio f32(300/1000) = 0.3 -> water used trunc(1000 x 0.3) = 300. End of pass: post 0x6946DC34, then the history in the order of 6.7 (produced 1000, consumed 300, imported 0, exported 0, pipes 5, unused 0, watered building cells 1, unwatered 0), MarkDealsDirty, post 0xEA418D8F / 8. State 5 sets every pipe watered. State 6 resets the scanning iterator at its end and state 7 runs it to the end again, so after the pass it is done at (0, 64) = (x0, countZ): GetNext after the last cell sets x := 0, z := 64 > z1 and then done (6.6, simgrid 7.4, PL4; this vector said (0, 63) before the spec answer). The redisplay box spans the changed cells: x from 0 (ring 5 at (0,5)) to 15, z from 0 to 11. Test 10: the consumption raised to 1200 (read live by BuildingConsumption) exceeds the supply 1000 at (12,5): consumed := 1000, the flood stops, (12,5) is not watered (value 2) and the ring-4 cell (13,5) is never reached; water used trunc(1000 x 1.0) = 1000; history consumed 1000, watered 0, unwatered 1.",
